<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:57:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Government expecting increased tax revenue in 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:656304364f4676baa8e48c9cbf829178bc7dcb1d91570e33ba09bfe2913f7cb9</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628--139a0de86753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finance Minister Lars Klingbeil said state tax revenue will increase by €4 billion in 2027. Meanwhile, public service websites have been coming back online after a PHP security scare. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Gandhi's nephew forced to pull protest photos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:174635ff9c001574f852ce1076db6a9e4e39babc9ab65cb7e4647412fbf74481</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462--8042d9d73860.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The requested removal of "objectionable" photos from a cultural center took place in state run by Modi's BJP. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France confirms first Shamonda virus infection in a human death of 'severely immunocompromised' individual</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d838dfa2e96eef0c442855cf9565df49a5956e9ba7f0a8d19061173b74738796</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-confirms-first-shamonda-virus-infection-in-a-human-death-of-severely-immunocompromised-indivi/a-79731991--31f7ca31d255.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-confirms-first-shamonda-virus-infection-in-a-human-death-of-severely-immunocompromised-individual/a-79731991?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Shomonda virus has been detected in a human for the first time, French health officials said. Authorities see no risk to the public, adding that the victim, who died in early October, was severely immunocompromised.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Balochistan border region sees growing unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:468252726aa85416bbf3aced5639cd24ee469c21b0cc817eed8260616f3dbf69</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399--7cda0ee86ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Violence is on the rise in Iran's border region with Afghanistan and Pakistan. The Iran war could shift the strategic balance for militant groups operating in the area.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Life near the front line in Sloviansk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:162b820e74d9542dec0787e85fce2aa6d04d882cae0585542aa17304c3fe84ed</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636--5ef08a6d884a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russian continues to attack Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine, thousands of residents refuse to leave or struggle to find a way out. For many, poverty, family ties and beloved pets make evacuation painfully difficult.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany arrests Ukrainian man suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0342456949908cbd37535ce6b842d913dcc13f694a021af89a3437986f1d6432</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373--a3202cca0fcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The suspect is thought to have gathered defense-related information on the production of tanks and munitions, as well as details about NATO's eastern flank.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU's Sakharov Prize won by the International Criminal Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:678070911f5604c10c5da9cd77347e9d810ae593ccdcad4ec01d3cc17ea17e5c</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-sakharov-prize-won-by-the-international-criminal-court/a-79730914--66e722beb7e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-sakharov-prize-won-by-the-international-criminal-court/a-79730914?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has announced the International Criminal Court as the winner of this year's Sakharov Prize. The annual prize is awarded to individuals and organizations for their work in supporting human rights and democracy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany overhaul its economy before AfD grows stronger?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b257f40fcacf0dbc8c2ca096b677f7b58fd69f1077b3c3b2c8f7523e68355e59</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102--b0df844ba99a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Which new sectors could revive growth and contain the far-right AfD, whose support has grown larger than ever?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4178a155c407ed7820c4ffa6c0dcdc47b65e4a9b251f9980ad7b611ebf296b80</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The most prestigious individual prize in football will be awarded on Monday, with Bayern Munich's English striker Harry Kane the front runner. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Concerns about security in the Black Sea dominate presidential election campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2d5c6b840c6812af23f835d2b701e9e39eae39a008cdae03a58c21337be0e3c</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094--fc0e44625feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgaria's presidential election campaign has been shaped by recent drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea and the government's reduced support for Ukraine, making foreign policy a key factor in the first round.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa CDC calls crisis meeting as Ebola spreads</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f9348253fbc6319832c38b958c8bdfc4ac21d648a95eb3eb8b2186ec7519d32</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-cdc-calls-crisis-meeting-as-ebola-spreads/a-79728604--521b9bc7db1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-cdc-calls-crisis-meeting-as-ebola-spreads/a-79728604?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">African health officials will hold a crisis meeting as the Ebola outbreak spreads from Congo to neighboring countries and beyond. The "extraordinary virtual meeting" will convene on October 28.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a28f16933e84e9d4e761d6c0148882b1d22aaa3344c6a87711d52c4d808ea56</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:57:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia trade strikes after Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04db67e1db2ab3027d22b006ee110006b0edf84cfafdf0be78a11f62bd5c220e</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T04:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-trade-strikes-after-witkoff-talks/a-79727542--9a5da82ad2b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-trade-strikes-after-witkoff-talks/a-79727542?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Soon after Putin and Zelenskyy expressed willingness to resume US-mediated talks, Russia and Ukraine traded major attacks on each other's capitals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Austrian, Swiss women kidnapped in Niger are freed — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f122bac1788ecf2e8bcde72921a3f6a674c8317f53195a0b91affe929c61a4c0</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T02:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austrian-swiss-women-kidnapped-in-niger-are-freed-report/a-79727419--97b94dcfa335.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austrian-swiss-women-kidnapped-in-niger-are-freed-report/a-79727419?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An Austrian woman and a Swiss woman kidnapped in Niger have been freed after 18 months in captivity, local reports say.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US orders some diplomats to leave Saudi Arabia amid Houthi threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8e0eeb885528d7be38e4c46ad1e83d096404c73b4b9635da09a81ab971bac17</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T01:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-orders-some-diplomats-to-leave-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-threat/a-79727353--5b66ad944bdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-orders-some-diplomats-to-leave-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-threat/a-79727353?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US State Department has asked some US diplomats to leave Saudi Arabia because of the threat of Houthi attacks on the Gulf kingdom.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo will not need further cancer treatment — Vatican</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b144b754cfa429672d09337dea11d8a1d5b5c9bb1e5925ea7354d8d0f2e4ac54</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T23:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-will-not-need-further-cancer-treatment-vatican/a-79727154--26d8f3c3281e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-will-not-need-further-cancer-treatment-vatican/a-79727154?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo's lung cancer surgery last week was a success, the Vatican said. The pope broke with traditions of secrecy around papal health issues after announcing he needed surgery to remove a nodule on his lung.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German youth plan France-style mass protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c0ea145d8793a85b2746be2fb8a00f9bf568f2afb8766d2af48cbc93f8cc2fa</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T23:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-youth-plan-france-style-mass-protests/a-79727133--417332c907bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-youth-plan-france-style-mass-protests/a-79727133?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A youth-led movement in Germany has called for demonstrations in major cities of the country on October 31. The group has categorically distanced itself from the violence that took hold in France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France bans protests in parts of Paris as Macron slams Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10fee79816c977e449e226b518eb643bc96298cdea3e8208de5334d1f3b60619</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-bans-protests-in-parts-of-paris-as-macron-slams-trump/a-79727141--35e37f1f4fe8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-bans-protests-in-parts-of-paris-as-macron-slams-trump/a-79727141?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron railed against "stupid" comments made by foreign leaders for their political purposes. Plus, Paris police are set to extend restrictions on gatherings in parts of the city on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: AfD's Weidel calls for major EU reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bded087234a602697cc5449d862b5d0540cab60ab45ecea6dae038830260576</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483--29b68ddcd610.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right Alternative for Germany co-leader Alice Weidel reveals the party's plan to reform the EU. Meanwhile, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang was in Berlin to talk to developers and investors. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Putin and Xi at one table, without Ukraine. What Moscow wants from the proposal and why Beijing might agree.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:112c71b2d54cbdd2e06023619748a898dcc38cda777c17b9d980d4177d1a2b06</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-/a-79726190--eeff17927fb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-might-agree/a-79726190?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is pushing for a summit with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping to discuss ending the war in Ukraine, without Kyiv or the EU. What does Russia hope to gain, and why might China be willing to take part?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Meta ordered to pay $25 billion in Cambridge Analytica case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f75d9bd4c23be74a8e2a8768f034ea4df2de9029b1e7bb3340581ff25f7c8d</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/meta-ordered-to-pay-25-billion-in-cambridge-analytica-case/a-79726486--b8819bb1d1ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/meta-ordered-to-pay-25-billion-in-cambridge-analytica-case/a-79726486?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A New Mexico judge ordered Facebook's parent company, Meta, to pay $25 billion for misleading users over the Cambridge Analytica breach, which took place during Donald Trump's first presidential campaign.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
